  "practice": [
    "Say ঊ three times with its modern u/oo sound: u, u, u.",
    "Practice ঊ-কার: ক + ূ = কূ, দ + ূ = দূ, ভ + ূ = ভূ, and প + ূ = পূ.",
    "Notice that ূ appears underneath its consonant and compare it with the short-vowel sign ু.",
    "Learn the spelling of common ূ words by sight: দূর, ভূত, মূল, সূর্য, and শূন্য."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ঊ is a Bengali vowel with an approximate u/oo sound.",
    "In modern spoken Bengali, উ and ঊ are generally pronounced the same; the main difference is spelling.",
    "When ঊ follows a consonant, it becomes ূ, called ঊ-কার, which appears underneath the consonant.",
    "The signs ু (উ-কার) and ূ (ঊ-কার) generally do not create a meaningful short-versus-long distinction in ordinary modern speech. Compare কুল and কূল, and learn the correct spelling with each word."
